# Overlay: drop CTS hardware flow control on the link to the nRF9151.
#
# Rationale
# ---------
# Flow control needs a third wire (nRF RTS -> ESP32 IO15) and that wire has
# been a persistent source of trouble on this breadboard build. It is also not
# strictly required here:
#
#   camera produces   ~40-50 kB/s at QVGA q12 / 15 fps
#   radio drains       ~63 kB/s
#   nRF RX ring         8 kB, DMA backed
#
# The receiver is faster than the sender, so back-pressure should never be
# needed in steady state. If it ever is, the nRF counts overruns and the PC
# decoder resynchronises on the next packet magic - a frame is lost, nothing
# breaks.
#
# With this overlay the link needs exactly two wires plus ground:
#   ESP32 IO13 -> nRF P0.02 (D2)   data
#   GND        <-> GND
#
# Build:
#   idf.py -B build_noflow -DSDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.noflow" \
#          -DSDKCONFIG=sdkconfig.noflow_gen build
CONFIG_DECTCAM_UART_FLOWCTRL=n
